---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "AI Workflow Consulting",
  "serviceType": "AI Consulting",
  "provider": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pravine Manivannan", "url": "https://pravinemani.com/" },
  "areaServed": "Worldwide",
  "description": "Production-grade AI workflows, custom MCP servers, agent systems, and prompt and eval suites. Built code-first on Claude Code and Vercel.",
  "url": "https://pravinemani.com/services/ai/"
};
---

<Base title="AI Workflow Consulting · Claude Code, MCP, Agents · Pravine Mani" description="Production AI workflows, custom MCP servers, agent systems and eval suites. Built code-first on Claude Code and Vercel. Toronto consultancy." jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/services/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">services</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <span class="you">ai</span>
  </div>
  <h1>AI workflows,<br><span class="accent">production-grade and code-first.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">AI workflows built in code on Claude Code, Vercel and Supabase. No no-code platforms, no monthly platform fee.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a href="/services/" class="cta-btn secondary">All engagement shapes</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-grid">

    <article class="vert-card" id="workflows">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">01</span><h2>Workflow automation</h2></div>
      <p>Repetitive work like lead routing, inbox triage, daily briefings and weekly reporting, turned into automations that run on a schedule. Written as code in your repo, not glued together in Zapier.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Runs on infrastructure you already own. No extra subscriptions.</li>
        <li>Validated outputs, so downstream systems don't break on bad data</li>
        <li>You own the code: versioned in git, debuggable, yours to change</li>
        <li>Two weeks of post-launch support</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="mcp">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">02</span><h2>Custom MCP servers</h2></div>
      <p>An MCP server lets Claude work directly with your CRM, database and internal APIs, with no copy-pasting context into a chat window. The AI calls your systems the way a teammate would.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your APIs, database queries and tools exposed as actions the AI can take safely</li>
        <li>Every request signed and verified, so nothing untrusted reaches your data</li>
        <li>A reusable template repo your team can extend without me</li>
        <li>Optional Claude Code skills, so your team installs the workflow with one command</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="agents">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">03</span><h2>Agent systems</h2></div>
      <p>For Orbit Dental I shipped a code-owned AI voice agent on Supabase Edge Functions that calls and qualifies new leads. A set of AI agents that handle multi-step work: research, planning, execution and review, with cost limits, error recovery and a record of every decision.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Specialized agents that hand work to each other, not one bloated prompt</li>
        <li>Hard spend ceilings per task and per user, so a runaway loop can't blow your bill</li>
        <li>A log of what each agent did, why, and what it cost</li>
        <li>For deeper concurrency work, see <a href="/services/agentic-os/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Agentic OS</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="evals">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">04</span><h2>Prompt + eval suites</h2></div>
      <p>A test suite for your AI features: real inputs, expected outputs, scored on every code change. It's the difference between "the demo worked" and "it kept working in production."</p>
      <ul>
        <li>30 to 100 test cases written from your real product traffic, not invented</li>
        <li>Every change runs the suite. If quality drops, the deploy is blocked.</li>
        <li>Prompts treated like code: versioned, reviewable, rolled back when needed</li>
        <li>You keep the test harness and can extend it</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="title-block">
      <div class="label">how it works</div>
      <h2>Engagement shapes for AI work.</h2>
      <p>The same paid engagement shapes apply across every focus area. Full ladder at <a href="/services/">/services</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="vert-engagements">
    <a href="/services/#pilot" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">PILOT BUILD</span><span class="when">FIXED PRICE · $750</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#sprint" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">BUILD SPRINT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE BUILD · QUOTE ON SCOPE</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#custom" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">CUSTOM BUILD</span><span class="when">MULTI-WORKFLOW · MILESTONE-PAID</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#retainer" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">OPS RETAINER</span><span class="when">MONTHLY · POST-ENGAGEMENT ONLY</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-cta reveal" style="text-align: center;">
    <p style="margin: 0;">Working on something AI-shaped? <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Send the problem →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
